Gamma-undecalactone has a molecular weight of 184.27 Da, while Diethyl isobutylmalonate has a molecular weight of 173.02 Da. Therefore, Gamma-undecalactone is heavier.

Note: The reported molecular weight for Diethyl isobutylmalonate (173.02 Da) seems lower than the expected value for this compound (typically ~216.3 Da based on its standard formula C11H20O4), so this value may warrant verification.

